<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Austro-Hungarian%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Austro-Hungarian Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The empire dissolves; armistice of Villa Giusti signed on 3 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Kiel mutiny sparks revolution; Wilhelm II abdicates and the armistice follows</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Margraviate%20of%20Moravia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Margraviate of Moravia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Moravia becomes a land of the new Czechoslovakia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bohemia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bohemia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Czechoslovakia is proclaimed in Prague, with Bohemia at its core</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wurttemberg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20W%C3%BCrttemberg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Württemberg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King William II renounces the throne on 30 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Grand%20Duchy%20of%20Hesse.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Grand Duchy of Hesse</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ernest Louis is declared deposed on 9 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bavaria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bavaria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kurt Eisner proclaims a republic in Munich and Ludwig III flees</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-sfsr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20SFSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian SFSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The capital moves to Moscow and the first Soviet constitution is adopted</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-finland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Finland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Finland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Whites under Mannerheim win the Finnish Civil War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Council of Lithuania signs the Act of Independence on 16 February</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes is proclaimed in Belgrade</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/czechoslovakia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Czechoslovakia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Czechoslovakia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence proclaimed in Prague on 28 October; Masaryk becomes president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Estonia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Estonia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Salvation Committee declares the Republic of Estonia on 24 February</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Latvia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Latvia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The People's Council proclaims the Republic of Latvia on 18 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/hyderabad-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hyderabad%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hyderabad State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mir Osman Ali Khan founds Osmania University</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-west-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20West%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French West Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Blaise Diagne leads a recruitment drive for the First World War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/womens-suffrage-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Women's%20suffrage%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Women's suffrage movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain gives the vote to women over 30 who meet a property qualification</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/aristocracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aristocracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aristocracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Revolution topples the German and Austrian monarchies, sweeping away noble chambers such as the Prussian House of Lords</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/one-party-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/One-party%20state.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>One-party state</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bolsheviks dissolve the Constituent Assembly and expel rival socialist parties from the soviets</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The German and Austrian monarchies fall and both countries are proclaimed republics</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/may-fourth-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/May%20Fourth%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>May Fourth Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The leak of the secret Sino-Japanese Joint Defence Agreement signed by Premier Duan Qirui sparks a student protest movement</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/young-turks"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Young%20Turks.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Young Turks</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The CUP ministry resigns, the Armistice of Mudros is signed, and Enver, Talaat and Cemal flee into exile</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Russian Social Democratic Labour Party renames itself the All-Russian Communist Party, setting communist apart from socialist</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/feminism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Feminism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Feminism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Representation of the People Act gives the vote to British women over 30 who own property</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-state-of-prussia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20State%20of%20Prussia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free State of Prussia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 12 November representatives of the Berlin workers' and soldiers' councils declare the previous Prussian government deposed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-romania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Romania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Romania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Representatives of the Transylvanian Romanians at Alba Iulia proclaim the union of Transylvania with Romania</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-serbia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Serbia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Serbia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 1 December Serbia unites with the State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs to form the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania-1918-1940"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania%20(1918-1940).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania (1918-1940)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 16 February the Council of Lithuania adopts the Act of Independence of Lithuania</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tibet-1912-1951"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tibet%20(1912-1951).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tibet (1912-1951)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lhasa regained control of Chamdo and western Kham, and a truce set the border at the Yangtze River</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/weimar-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Weimar%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Weimar Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Philipp Scheidemann proclaims the German Republic in Berlin and the abdication of Kaiser Wilhelm II is announced</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/second-polish-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Polish%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Polish Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Regency Council announces the restoration of Polish independence on 7 October, and on 14 November transfers its authority to Józef Piłsudski as Chief of State</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-caporetto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Caporetto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Caporetto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Italians defeat the Austro-Hungarian army at Vittorio Veneto, and an armistice is signed on 3 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/moscow"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Moscow.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Moscow</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lenin moves the capital back to Moscow on 12 March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/saint-petersburg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saint%20Petersburg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saint Petersburg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lenin moves the Soviet government to Moscow</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/warsaw"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Warsaw.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Warsaw</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Warsaw becomes the capital of independent Poland</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/ishtar-gate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ishtar%20Gate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ishtar Gate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the First World War ended, the smaller frontal gate was reconstructed in the Pergamon Museum in Berlin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/vladimir-lenin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vladimir%20Lenin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vladimir Lenin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Russia signs the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk, the Red Terror begins, and Lenin is shot and severely wounded by Fanny Kaplan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/march-first-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/March%20First%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>March First Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the end of the First World War, Woodrow Wilson announces the Fourteen Points, including national self-determination</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/maori-king-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/M%C4%81ori%20King%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Māori King movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Police arrest men at Te Paina who failed to report for military duty under conscription</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/new-culture-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Culture%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Culture Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lu Xun publishes Diary of a Madman, which implies that China's traditional culture was mentally cannibalistic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-slavism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Slavism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Slavism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Kingdom of Yugoslavia unites most South Slavic-speaking nations under the Karađorđević dynasty</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/gandhism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gandhism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gandhism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gandhi issues two public appeals for Indians to enlist in the British Indian Army in the First World War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/native-american-church"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Native%20American%20Church.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Native American Church</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Native American Church is officially created</span></li></ul></section>
